     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Martin,<div><br>Before you post, check carefully the lines of code you are submitting. When you make an assignment, try printing the output and ask yourself &quot;does this give me what I think it is giving me? <br>You are trying to set the strata from data.frame(other(martin25)). What is in `other(martin25)`? Likely, there is nothing there. <br>Read <a href=\"https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Population_Strata.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Population_Strata.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480006178000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1g6c0AjqODrZOKFmM47YVD\">https://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R/Population_Strata.html</a> and see if that clears up the question about strata.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Zhian</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
